The LikeOS libc has neither O_DIRECT nor EBADFD.

  O_DIRECT: mkfs.exfat --verify re-reads what it wrote with the device
      switched to O_DIRECT so that the read cannot be served from a page
      cache.  LikeOS block device nodes have no page cache in front of
      them (every read() goes to the drive), so a plain read verifies the
      same thing; the fcntl() is left out where O_DIRECT is not defined.
  EBADFD: the "no /dev/zero descriptor" error of the zero-page mapping
      helper becomes EBADF (the descriptor is not valid), the nearest
      code the libc has.

